abstract: >
  Self-contained prediction guarantees for two interpretations of the
  two-sided majority with a 60/40 gap from Blum and Balcan (COLT 2007):
  a dimension-independent perceptron bound for the group-normalized promise,
  a distribution-free counting inequality for the active-normalized promise,
  a polynomial-time signed-literal learner, and NP-completeness of exact
  partition compatibility. Includes LaTeX source, Python code, reproducible
  finite checks, and internal AI-assisted audit reports.
keywords:
  - semi-supervised learning
  - PAC learning
  - majority with margins
  - perceptron
  - sample compression
  - NP-completeness
